0..78 Comment "// A program encloses the square root of two through `std.reals.Eff`, the host"
79..107 Comment "// interface of exact reals."
108..110 Comment "//"
111..183 Comment "// The program gives the host the canonical bytes of a plan in lowercase"
184..262 Comment "// hexadecimal. The plan holds one cut, the square root of two, whose laws are"
263..339 Comment "// the registered cut of stage A. The host validates the bytes and replies a"
340..414 Comment "// plan. The program then asks for an enclosure no wider than `2^-64`. The"
415..491 Comment "// checker replays the certificate of the enclosure before the host replies."
492..494 Comment "//"
495..574 Comment "// `gandr run sqrt-two.gandr` prints the lower end and then the upper end. Each"
575..652 Comment "// end has the form `<mantissa>p<exponent>` for `mantissa · 2^exponent`. The"
653..730 Comment "// same `enclosed` runs under a handler of this source, a second model of the"
731..744 Comment "// interface."
745..747 Comment "//"
748..825 Comment "// - see: `crates/surface-dispatcher/src/evaluate/reals.rs` — the host that"
826..851 Comment "//   serves the interface"
852..930 Comment "// - see: `crates/theory-exact-reals/README.md` — the plans, the machine and"
931..947 Comment "//   the checker"
949..981 Comment "// The console\'s host interface."
